Result

The MD5 data transformation process was studied using the Virtual Lab. The input message was processed through the simulation stages, and the final 128-bit hash value was displayed.

Conclusion

The experiment demonstrated the basic working of the MD5 hashing algorithm, including message padding, initialization, nonlinear functions, buffer operations, constants and circular shifts. It showed how an input message is transformed into a fixed-length hash value.

